# Build output
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/
_deps/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CTestTestfile.cmake
install_manifest.txt
compile_commands.json
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.exe

# Benchmark output. Raw sample files are large and are regenerated by a run;
# what belongs in git is the summary table in RESULTS.md and the figures a
# reviewer actually looks at.
data/*.csv
data/*.json
perf.data
perf.data.old
callgrind.out.*
cachegrind.out.*

# Keep the generated figures and summary tables — they are small, they are
# referenced from RESULTS.md, and GitHub renders them.
!docs/figures/*.png

# The built dashboard is a generated artifact: a quarter-megabyte of minified
# JSON inlined into one HTML file, which GitHub cannot render and no one should
# read as source. What is tracked is everything needed to rebuild it —
# docs/dashboard.template.html, docs/figures/dashboard_data.json, and the two
# scripts. Rebuild with:  python3 scripts/build_dashboard.py
docs/dashboard.html

# Editors and local tooling
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python (scripts/plot.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Source material for the build plan. Useful to keep locally, but the repo
# should present the work rather than the study plan behind it. Delete these
# two lines if you would rather ship them.
order_book_build_manual.pdf
files.zip
